# The full container run at 021b5453: 34 gates green, including the two that were red last time (2026-10-04)

`scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --full` was run end to end against the committed tree at
`021b5453`, the commit that gave both gate runners a `--only`, mirrored `RUST_MIN_STACK`
into the host runner, and fixed the two shell scripts that died before printing a report. It
came back `all gates passed in chaos-verify:frozen` with exit code 0.

That matters because the same command at the previous two commits ended `FAILED gates: cargo
clippy cargo test` -- see `docs/verification/verify-in-docker-full-8a52ff0a-2026-10-04.log`,
where both reds were defects in a test that commit had just shipped. Here both of those
gates pass, so the workspace builds warning-free under `-D warnings` and the whole `cargo
test --workspace --locked --no-fail-fast` leg is green in a container that started from
`debian:bookworm-slim`.

The 3.0 MB / 35 736-line transcript is not committed. Everything quoted below is copied out
of it, and the last section gives the commands to reproduce the run and to re-measure the
counts.

== 0. Where the run sits, and why not in the working tree

Same arrangement as `docs/verification/verify-in-docker-full-a04e91a7-2026-10-04.log`
section 0: the script bind-mounts the repository root it was invoked from and fingerprints
the working tree before and after, so a sweep that describes a commit has to run from a tree
that is nothing but that commit. On 2026-10-04 that became less necessary -- `.dockerignore`
makes the entry point cheap enough to run from a live tree, and a `--only` run from one is
recorded in `docs/verification/pipefail-report-gate-2026-10-04.log` section 8 -- but a full
sweep still does not belong next to an editor.

    $ cd /var/tmp/verify-frozen-a04e91a7
    $ git fetch -q origin main && git checkout -q --detach 021b5453
    $ git log --oneline -1
    021b5453 fix(ci,installer,shell): 三处「退出码对了、报告没了」的缺陷，加两个 runner 的 --only 与环境镜像
    $ git status --porcelain | head -3
    $ IMAGE_TAG=chaos-verify:frozen ./scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --full > "$L" 2>&1

The empty `git status` line before the run is what makes the checksum below a claim about
`021b5453` rather than about whatever was in the way.

== 1. The verdict, as printed

    == preparing cargo cache volumes
    == source tree: 4006 files, checksum 2419869843

    == preflight: container can read the repository
    preflight: OK

    == toolchain matches the pin
    rustc 1.94.0 (4a4ef493e 2026-03-02)
    cargo 1.94.0 (85eff7c80 2026-01-15)

    == pinned protoc launcher
    libprotoc 29.3

    ...

    GUI protocol types are up to date

    all gates passed in chaos-verify:frozen

and the exit code, from the `echo` appended to the command rather than from the script:

    DOCKER-FULL-EXIT=0

The run printed no `UNATTRIBUTABLE` line. The script recomputes the same checksum after the
last gate and says that only on a mismatch, so its absence is the statement that all 34
gates belong to the tree whose checksum is 2419869843 and that nothing moved while they ran:

    $ grep -c UNATTRIBUTABLE "$L"
    0

Elapsed time was 2 140 seconds (35 minutes 40 seconds), from the transcript's creation to
its last write (`stat` birth 12:36:06, mtime 12:57:46), which is the wall clock of a
cold-ish clippy leg on top of a warm cargo volume.

== 2. Which gates ran

`--full` appends `cargo test` and `GUI protocol types` to the array, so the run selected 34
labels. Every one of them appears as its own `== <label>` heading, checked by driving the
label list rather than by counting heading lines (several gate commands print their own `==`
headings, so a bare count of those is 41 and means nothing):

    $ bash scripts/verify-gates.sh --list | while IFS= read -r lab; do
          grep -q "^== ${lab}$" "$L" || echo "missing: $lab"
      done
    missing: pipefail report

That one absence is the only difference, and it is expected: the `pipefail report` gate
arrived in the working tree after `021b5453` and is measured on its own in
`docs/verification/pipefail-report-gate-2026-10-04.log`. The other `==` lines in the
transcript, `== the release version and everything that must equal it` among them, are
output written by `scripts/ci/check-versions.sh` and
`scripts/ci/test-installer-asset-names.py`, not gate headings.

== 3. The two gates that were red at 8a52ff0a

`cargo clippy` compiles the workspace with `-D warnings` and prints nothing but cargo's own
progress lines. Its section ends:

    == cargo clippy
       Compiling xai-grok-pager-bin v0.4.2 (/src/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager-bin)
        Checking xai-grok-shell v0.4.2 (/src/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell)
        Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized] target(s) in 1m 21s

and the transcript contains no diagnostic at all, which is the check:

    $ grep -cE '^(error|warning):' "$L"
    0

`cargo test --workspace --locked --no-fail-fast` runs to completion with no failing test
binary:

    $ grep -c '^test result:' "$L"
    386
    $ grep -E '^test result: FAILED' "$L" | grep -c ''
    0

Re-adding the counts across those 386 result lines, unit tests, integration tests and the 95
doc-test crates together:

    test result lines: 386  passed=31594 failed=0 ignored=485  doc-test crates=95

The 485 ignored tests are the population that `scripts/ci/ignored-tests-baseline.tsv`
accounts for; the `ignored-test baseline` gate is one of the 34 and passed in this same run,
so the number is not new debt, it is the recorded debt.

== 4. What this run does not establish

It is Linux-only platform evidence. It says nothing about the macOS or Windows code paths,
about signing, about installers, or about a real TLS-terminating deployment, and it is not a
substitute for the CI run of the same commit, which additionally runs the GUI browser E2E
and the frontend jobs.

It also predates the gate this batch adds. The `pipefail report` gate was still uncommitted
while this ran, so its 34-gate result and the 1-gate `--only` run are two separate pieces of
evidence and are quoted separately, not merged into a claim that "35 gates passed".

Finally, a green `cargo test` under `--no-fail-fast` on this machine does not retire the
known load-sensitive cases: the platform leg's ignored-test list and the `--full`-only
timing assumptions in `CONTRIBUTING.md` still stand as written.

== 5. Reproduce it

    # from a clone detached at the commit, with the tree at rest
    cd /var/tmp/verify-frozen-a04e91a7
    git fetch -q origin main && git checkout -q --detach 021b5453
    IMAGE_TAG=chaos-verify:frozen ./scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --full \
      > /tmp/verify-full-021b5453.log 2>&1; echo "DOCKER-FULL-EXIT=$?"

    # the verdict and the two gates that were red at 8a52ff0a
    tail -3 /tmp/verify-full-021b5453.log
    grep -cE '^(error|warning):' /tmp/verify-full-021b5453.log
    grep -c '^test result:' /tmp/verify-full-021b5453.log

    # every label ran
    bash scripts/verify-gates.sh --list | while IFS= read -r lab; do
      grep -q "^== ${lab}$" /tmp/verify-full-021b5453.log || echo "missing: $lab"
    done
